      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ec1bdbe8-6790-5414-8c3d-a07807c0ae92",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marcia Wallace, Edna Krabappel, Lance Kramer, David Silverman, Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Maggie Roswell, Russi Taylor, Tom Hanks, Albert Brooks, Ned Flanders, Bart Simpson\n- Works: The Bob Newhart Show, The Simpsons, The Simpsons Movie\n- Roles: Carol Kester, elementary school teacher, receptionist, additional sequence director\n- Organizations/Places: Springfield Elementary School\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1970s, Marcia Wallace played receptionist Carol Kester on the sitcom \"The Bob Newhart Show\".\n- In 1992, Marcia Wallace won an Emmy for voicing Edna Krabappel on \"The Simpsons\".\n- Edna Krabappel is Bart Simpson's 4th grade teacher at Springfield Elementary School in \"The Simpsons\".\n- In later seasons of \"The Simpsons\", Edna Krabappel becomes Ned Flanders's wife.\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" was directed by David Silverman.\n- Lance Kramer served as an additional sequence director for \"The Simpsons Movie\".\n- Marcia Wallace was part of the regular television cast featured in \"The Simpsons Movie\", alongside Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Maggie Roswell, and Russi Taylor.\n- \"The Simpsons Movie\" also featured Tom Hanks, Green Day, and Albert Brooks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "89e1e5cb-cf0c-5b88-b16b-8606f6f3ea8f",
        "text": "Page: Marcia Wallace. Sentence: She is perhaps best known for her roles as receptionist Carol Kester on the 1970s sitcom \"The Bob Newhart Show\", and as the voice of elementary school teacher Edna Krabappel on the animated series \"The Simpsons\", for which she won an Emmy in 1992.\nPage: Edna Krabappel. Sentence: She is the teacher of Bart Simpson's 4th grade class at Springfield Elementary School, and Ned Flanders's wife in later seasons.\nPage: The Simpsons Movie. Sentence: The film was directed by David Silverman, and stars the regular television cast of Dan Castellaneta, Julie Kavner, Nancy Cartwright, Yeardley Smith, Hank Azaria, Harry Shearer, Tress MacNeille, Pamela Hayden, Marcia Wallace, Maggie Roswell and Russi Taylor, along with Tom Hanks, Green Day and Albert Brooks.\nPage: Lance Kramer. Sentence: He was as an additional sequence director for \"The Simpsons Movie\".",
